---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import headshot from '../assets/henard-gertzen.png';
import { pages, site } from '../site';

const meta = pages['/about/'];
const article = 'https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/lazy-optimizer-why-we-need-stop-calling-ai-henard-gertzen-dnpef/';
---

<Base title={meta.title} description={meta.description} image="/og/about.png">
  <div class="wrap about">
    <header class="about-head">
      <h1>About me</h1>
    </header>

    <aside class="about-aside" aria-label="At a glance">
      <figure class="portrait">
        <Image
          src={headshot}
          alt="Henard Gertzen, smiling, in a white shirt and tie"
          widths={[200, 400]}
          sizes="(min-width: 52rem) 13rem, 7rem"
          loading="eager"
        />
      </figure>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div>
          <dt>Based in</dt>
          <dd>Secunda, South Africa</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Works on</dt>
          <dd>.NET, Angular, Claude Code</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Studied</dt>
          <dd>BSc IT, North-West University</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Speaks</dt>
          <dd>English, Afrikaans, some Dutch</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Elsewhere</dt>
          <dd>
            <a href={site.links.linkedin} rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>,
            <a href={site.links.github} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </aside>

    <div class="about-body">
      <p class="lede">
        I’m a full-stack developer in Secunda, South Africa. I help teams get coding agents to write code that fits
        their codebase, not just code that compiles.
      </p>
      <p>
        I wrote my first software in high school, as one of a handful of students in the first year group at my
        school to take IT, and built my first WordPress websites in holiday jobs. After school I worked as a hardware
        technician, keeping clients’ systems up to date.
      </p>
      <p>
        In 2021 I started a BSc in IT at North-West University in Potchefstroom. Alongside my studies I did freelance
        graphic and web design, and helped other students set up their computers, learn their software and get
        through their projects. In my final year I led our team on <a href="/projects/#share2teach">Share2Teach</a> as
        team lead, Scrum Master and head designer.
      </p>
      <p>
        After graduating I spent a few months as an intermediate full-stack developer at EziDev, then moved back to
        Secunda. Today I work remotely as a full-stack developer on .NET and Angular software, specialising in AI
        harnesses: the setup that makes coding agents work to a team’s standards.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside work I build <a href="/projects/#games-title">games with coding agents</a>, a point-of-sale system,
        and software for philosophy and theology. I think a lot about what AI actually is and the role agents play in
        our lives, and I’ve written about <a href={article}>why I’d rather call it a lazy optimizer than intelligent</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The best way to reach me is <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, or see
        <a href="/contact/">what I do</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
